00:53:45.900 --> 00:53:49.670
What is important to have this
connection between discussed--

00:53:49.670 --> 00:53:54.270
so you were mentioning that in
the formation of the universe.

00:53:54.270 --> 00:53:57.770
So you have two stars that
they might be connected or have

00:53:57.770 --> 00:53:58.380
connection?

00:53:58.380 --> 00:54:00.090
Is that important?

00:54:00.090 --> 00:54:03.440
So I mean, is it important?

00:54:03.440 --> 00:54:05.870
We try to find out
what it is, right?

00:54:05.870 --> 00:54:07.800
The universe is what it is.

00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:10.460
We're not going to
make a new universe.

00:54:10.460 --> 00:54:15.530
But in this particular
case, and it won't be stars,

00:54:15.530 --> 00:54:16.430
it'd be galaxies.

00:54:16.430 --> 00:54:18.390
But I mean, the same idea.

00:54:18.390 --> 00:54:19.640
You have two objects.

00:54:19.640 --> 00:54:22.370
And if these two objects
can't talk to each other

00:54:22.370 --> 00:54:24.920
because there wasn't enough
time for them to exchange

00:54:24.920 --> 00:54:27.410
light or information-- no
information travels faster

00:54:27.410 --> 00:54:28.640
than light, we think.

00:54:28.640 --> 00:54:30.920
If there was no time to
exchange information,

00:54:30.920 --> 00:54:34.380
they shouldn't be
related to each other.

00:54:34.380 --> 00:54:36.700
They should have
formed independently.

00:54:36.700 --> 00:54:39.410
Because if they're
related to each other,

00:54:39.410 --> 00:54:40.960
let's say, if this star--

00:54:40.960 --> 00:54:41.770
the stars, right?

00:54:41.770 --> 00:54:43.390
If this star
evaporates that one,

00:54:43.390 --> 00:54:46.980
light needs to have time to
go from this one to that one.

00:54:46.980 --> 00:54:48.730
Otherwise, it can't
evaporate or the light

00:54:48.730 --> 00:54:51.010
can't make it because the
universe isn't old enough yet.

00:54:51.010 --> 00:54:53.260
Now, this I'm going to be stars
because the universe grows

00:54:53.260 --> 00:54:53.780
pretty fast.

00:54:53.780 --> 00:54:55.940
It's going to be galaxies
that talk to each other.

00:54:55.940 --> 00:54:59.020
But the same idea is if
they form like a structure,

00:54:59.020 --> 00:55:03.040
like a perfect ring on
the sky, then that ring

00:55:03.040 --> 00:55:05.560
must have formed,
we think, at a time

00:55:05.560 --> 00:55:08.318
when there was some event
that made that ring.

00:55:08.318 --> 00:55:08.860
I don't know.

00:55:08.860 --> 00:55:10.360
Explosion in the
middle or something

00:55:10.360 --> 00:55:12.400
that made them all
form at the same time

00:55:12.400 --> 00:55:13.950
or something like that.

00:55:13.950 --> 00:55:17.070
If the structure formed when
the universe was so young

00:55:17.070 --> 00:55:19.805
that nothing could have gone
between here from there,

00:55:19.805 --> 00:55:23.140
why are they on
this perfect ring?

00:55:23.140 --> 00:55:25.810
What made them go on that ring?

00:55:25.810 --> 00:55:28.240
They should be randomly located.

00:55:28.240 --> 00:55:30.747
And the probability of
randomly making a ring

00:55:30.747 --> 00:55:32.830
or randomly making a
triangle or whatever you want

00:55:32.830 --> 00:55:33.920
is pretty low.

00:55:33.920 --> 00:55:36.220
So if you find
structures that look

00:55:36.220 --> 00:55:39.190
as if there is some
causality, some

00:55:39.190 --> 00:55:42.043
cause that made
this structure, then

00:55:42.043 --> 00:55:43.710
the universe should
have been old enough

00:55:43.710 --> 00:55:46.950
that cause can actually
propagate information

00:55:46.950 --> 00:55:51.210
from, I don't know, an
explosion or whatever it is.

00:55:51.210 --> 00:55:52.843
Let's take an explosion
as an example.

00:55:52.843 --> 00:55:55.260
Let's say there's an explosion
in the middle and the shock

00:55:55.260 --> 00:55:58.290
wave that comes out and
that forms something.

00:55:58.290 --> 00:56:00.422
Then, that can only
happen if-- when

00:56:00.422 --> 00:56:02.130
it formed, if the
universe was old enough

00:56:02.130 --> 00:56:04.810
for the shock to actually go
from the middle to the outside.

00:56:04.810 --> 00:56:05.990
Otherwise, that won't work.

00:56:05.990 --> 00:56:08.490
So if there's nothing can go
from the middle to the outside,

00:56:08.490 --> 00:56:11.400
how would we get like a
perfect ring of galaxies?

00:56:11.400 --> 00:56:13.410
That inflationary
rate of expansion

00:56:13.410 --> 00:56:19.710
was too far in the past to
have accounted for that.

00:56:19.710 --> 00:56:22.110
There are certainly things
that are related to that.

00:56:22.110 --> 00:56:24.900
There's some things called
baryon acoustic oscillations

00:56:24.900 --> 00:56:26.430
that have to do
with this inflation.

00:56:26.430 --> 00:56:28.200
But I'm not an
expert on inflation

00:56:28.200 --> 00:56:30.300
and I'm not going to
derive the equations

00:56:30.300 --> 00:56:32.910
of the inflationary universe
on a Blackboard now.

00:56:32.910 --> 00:56:35.310
Maybe Alan Guth will
respond at some point.

00:56:35.310 --> 00:56:36.180
Maybe.

00:56:36.180 --> 00:56:38.760
As I say, this particular
press release from last week,

00:56:38.760 --> 00:56:41.340
I'm sure lots of people
are going to look at it.

00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:46.240
We'll keep our
attention focused.

00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:46.850
OK.

00:56:46.850 --> 00:56:47.350
Thank you.

00:56:47.350 --> 00:56:48.020
Thank you.
Thank you.

00:56:48.020 --> 00:56:48.820
Thanks for coming.

